<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating (Protoreaster nodosus (Asteroidea) & Metacrinus rotundus / Nesometra integra (Crinoidea) / Cidaris rugosa (Echinoidea); larval spiculogenesis after Strongylocentrotus purpuratus (Echinoidea))",
        "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating faithfully reproduces Protoreaster nodosus (Asteroidea) & Metacrinus rotundus / Nesometra integra (Crinoidea) / Cidaris rugosa (Echinoidea); larval spiculogenesis after Strongylocentrotus purpuratus (Echinoidea) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-6> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Protoreaster nodosus (Asteroidea) & Metacrinus rotundus / Nesometra integra (Crinoidea) / Cidaris rugosa (Echinoidea); larval spiculogenesis after Strongylocentrotus purpuratus (Echinoidea) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 88.2/100, audit 2026-10-19-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py> ;
    schema:about "Protoreaster nodosus (Asteroidea) & Metacrinus rotundus / Nesometra integra (Crinoidea) / Cidaris rugosa (Echinoidea); larval spiculogenesis after Strongylocentrotus purpuratus (Echinoidea)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Reproduction of Yang et al. (2022) load-depth curves or twin-band micrographs; a physically faithful [111] projection (the Pass 2 projection integrates over a partial period and is flagged below); literature-digitised validation of the 12-species table (synthetic, flagged below); online-verified DOIs for the seven Pass 3 references",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 3D nodal TPMS level sets and implicit-surface curvature for Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P, a Cahn-Hilliard spinodal control and a pinch-off ablation (Pass 2); level-set threshold sweep; Gibson-Ashby stretching vs bending scaling; DoG segmentation of the vendored crinoid ossicle SEM plate (Pass 2)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Pass 3: a reduced 2D plane-strain Q4 crystal-plasticity FEM of flat-punch nanoindentation on the [111]-projected Diamond skeletal honeycomb section vs a monolith at equal depth with two e-twin variants, lamella run lengths by ray marching, pore-adjacent arrest fraction, r90 damage radius and P/P_elastic; an Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro pile-up scaling in strut / ossicle / monolith glide lengths; a stochastic 2D syncytial-templating model of ACC vesicle delivery with secondary vs primary nucleation and templating / nucleation ablations",
        "reported_in_source: Beniash et al. (1997), Politi et al. (2008), Vidavsky et al. (2014), Wilt (2002): sea urchin larval spicules are deposited as ACC delivered in ~1 um vesicles into a syncytial membrane cavity and transform to calcite by secondary nucleation propagating from a single seed granule",
        "reported_in_source: Donnay & Pawson (1969): every echinoderm skeletal element diffracts as a single calcite crystal",
        "reported_in_source: Eshelby, Frank & Nabarro (1951): a pile-up of n = pi(1-nu) L tau/(mu b) dislocations against an obstacle over a glide length L concentrates a head stress n tau",
        "reported_in_source: Yang et al. (2022): the ossicles of Protoreaster nodosus are single-crystal calcite shaped as a diamond-type TPMS lattice with [111] along the c-axis; under nanoindentation, twin bands and dislocations are arrested at the strut-pore free surfaces, confining damage to indent-adjacent struts (3D crystal-plasticity FEM in the paper)",
        "transfer_boundary: The FEM is a 2D plane-strain honeycomb section (bending-dominated; the 3D Diamond TPMS is stretching-dominated), with a single twin family (no r/f slip, both twin senses allowed via |tau|), isotropic elasticity for trigonal calcite, a flat punch rather than a Berkovich tip, no fracture coupling, and tau_twin = 500 MPa as a scale parameter (depth-normalised outputs are tau-invariant, absolute depths are not)",
        "transfer_boundary: The specimen plate is an adult Nesometra integra calyx ossicle; the slot organism is Metacrinus rotundus and the seed paper's organism is the starfish Protoreaster nodosus. The specimen reference values in the JSON (phi = 0.5187, a_0 = 14.80 um) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs, not independent literature values",
        "transfer_boundary: The templating model's kinetics (k_1, k_2, p_out, vesicle flux, front reach) are modelling choices not fitted to the Politi 2008 / Beniash 1997 ACC-fraction time courses; the template is the adult stereom honeycomb, not a larval triradiate spicule; no membrane mechanics or Mg/protein ACC stabilisation" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "8. Crystal Accretion & TPMS" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Coiled Shells, Spicules & Gyroids" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Raup (W,D,S) / Gyroid Mean H=0" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Metacrinus" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py; output: docs/media/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_comparison.png; organism: Protoreaster nodosus (Asteroidea) & Metacrinus rotundus / Nesometra integra (Crinoidea) / Cidaris rugosa (Echinoidea); larval spiculogenesis after Strongylocentrotus purpuratus (Echinoidea); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/9987db7d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: ac9f4ac4b8e557301e259e7d30ec4d97d4e8114ecfa867c705d25665fdc0a463; artifact_sha256: 108bc444ec648e58338e88b86748dfcde5d8cb560cbb23f515e41a09883e349e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json=c1c3848ef15d0bfc..., datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_ossicle_specimen.jpg=5fbf6e4db0ee1d44..., datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/nanoindentation_spiculogenesis_reference.json=f611bfb48faef772..., datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/scout_manifest.json=0524b76e141ef1fe...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Yang et al. (2022): the ossicles of Protoreaster nodosus are single-crystal calcite shaped as a diamond-type TPMS lattice with [111] along the c-axis; under nanoindentation, twin bands and dislocations are arrested at the strut-pore free surfaces, confining damage to indent-adjacent struts (3D crystal-plasticity FEM in the paper) | Donnay & Pawson (1969): every echinoderm skeletal element diffracts as a single calcite crystal | Beniash et al. (1997), Politi et al. (2008), Vidavsky et al. (2014), Wilt (2002): sea urchin larval spicules are deposited as ACC delivered in ~1 um vesicles into a syncytial membrane cavity and transform to calcite by secondary nucleation propagating from a single seed granule | Eshelby, Frank & Nabarro (1951): a pile-up of n = pi(1-nu) L tau/(mu b) dislocations against an obstacle over a glide length L concentrates a head stress n tau; reconstructed_in_script: 3D nodal TPMS level sets and implicit-surface curvature for Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P, a Cahn-Hilliard spinodal control and a pinch-off ablation (Pass 2); level-set threshold sweep; Gibson-Ashby stretching vs bending scaling; DoG segmentation of the vendored crinoid ossicle SEM plate (Pass 2) | Pass 3: a reduced 2D plane-strain Q4 crystal-plasticity FEM of flat-punch nanoindentation on the [111]-projected Diamond skeletal honeycomb section vs a monolith at equal depth with two e-twin variants, lamella run lengths by ray marching, pore-adjacent arrest fraction, r90 damage radius and P/P_elastic; an Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro pile-up scaling in strut / ossicle / monolith glide lengths; a stochastic 2D syncytial-templating model of ACC vesicle delivery with secondary vs primary nucleation and templating / nucleation ablations; transfer_boundary: The FEM is a 2D plane-strain honeycomb section (bending-dominated; the 3D Diamond TPMS is stretching-dominated), with a single twin family (no r/f slip, both twin senses allowed via |tau|), isotropic elasticity for trigonal calcite, a flat punch rather than a Berkovich tip, no fracture coupling, and tau_twin = 500 MPa as a scale parameter (depth-normalised outputs are tau-invariant, absolute depths are not) | The templating model's kinetics (k_1, k_2, p_out, vesicle flux, front reach) are modelling choices not fitted to the Politi 2008 / Beniash 1997 ACC-fraction time courses; the template is the adult stereom honeycomb, not a larval triradiate spicule; no membrane mechanics or Mg/protein ACC stabilisation | The specimen plate is an adult Nesometra integra calyx ossicle; the slot organism is Metacrinus rotundus and the seed paper's organism is the starfish Protoreaster nodosus. The specimen reference values in the JSON (phi = 0.5187, a_0 = 14.80 um) are the script's own Pass 2 outputs, not independent literature values; does_not_claim: Reproduction of Yang et al. (2022) load-depth curves or twin-band micrographs; a physically faithful [111] projection (the Pass 2 projection integrates over a partial period and is flagged below); literature-digitised validation of the 12-species table (synthetic, flagged below); online-verified DOIs for the seven Pass 3 references]" ;
