<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the header docstring (L1-80) maps Sections 4b and 6b to the ten sources and the six Lean theorems, states the reductions (2D, one twin family, no r/f slip, no fracture) and flags refs 5-10 as offline-recalled; function docstrings cite the equation or paper step for the FEM, pile-up and templating code; model constants carry inline provenance comments (L117-138); the math-KG YAML registers equations 5-6 with single-range lean_locus / code_locus. Deductions: the Pass 2 [111] projection docstring claims to follow Yang et al. Figs. 2-3 while the implementation integrates a partial period and the dislocation is an ansatz whose comment asserts a winding of 1.0 that is simply assigned (L552-555, L591-592) (-3); the E/10 'cleavage scale' line (L1714-1716) is a scale marker presented beside measured quantities (-1); DEFAULT_TAU_TWIN_MPA = 500 (L118) is a scale parameter whose role is explained in the comment but the pile-up head stress at this tau in a 6 um strut (147 GPa) is unphysical and not flagged in the panel (-1). Net -1 from v2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1714–L1716: e_cleave = E/10 drawn as a 'cleavage scale' marker — a scale line, not a measured cleavage stress <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1714-L1716>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L552–L555: DEFECT: docstring claims Yang et al. Figs. 2-3 projections while the code integrates a partial [111] period and hard-codes the Burgers winding <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L552-L555>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: the Pass 2 3D nodal TPMS level sets, implicit-surface H/K and odd-inversion/half-fraction results remain correct (L287-478); the new FEM implements a genuine small-strain crystal-plasticity scheme — Q4 plane-strain stiffness (L670-689), Schmid resolved shear on two e-twin variants, perfectly plastic criterion with twin-shear exhaustion, initial-strain iteration with a single LU factorisation per structure, displacement-controlled flat punch, lattice vs monolith at equal depth (L692-868, L908-974) — and the pile-up scaling is the Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro formula (L871-905); the templating model encodes the Politi secondary-nucleation vs primary-nucleation distinction and the Beniash / Vidavsky vesicle-delivery picture (L1155-1269). Deductions: the Pass 2 [111] projection integrates along w in [0, 2 pi) instead of the full [111] period 2 pi sqrt(3) (L558), so Panel D's hexagonal contrast is a partial-period artefact, and its edge dislocation is a phase-winding ansatz with burgers_winding = 1.0 hard-coded (L582-592) (-4); the FEM is a 2D plane-strain honeycomb section of a 3D stretching-dominated lattice with one twin family, |tau| used for both twin senses (L798-802), no r/f slip, isotropic elasticity and no fracture, so it cannot be compared with Yang et al.'s load-depth or twin-band data (-3); the templating kinetics are unfitted model choices and the template is the adult honeycomb rather than a larval triradiate spicule (-2). Net -2 from v2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L549–L603: DEFECT: [111] projection integrates w over [0, 2 pi) (L558) rather than the full 2 pi sqrt(3) period — projected D density is uniform over the full period; edge dislocation is an ansatz with burgers_winding = 1.0 hard-coded (L592) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L549-L603>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L798–L802: Twin criterion uses |tau| for both variants and both senses — calcite e-twinning is polar; no r/f slip <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L798-L802>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P), Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics, nanoindentation twin-band arrest FEM & syncytial ACC templating — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credit: `measure_morphoeval()` (L1842-2028) now returns 16 reference-anchored measurements; the 7 new ones (L1863-1934) report a non-trivial FEM result (max lamella 2.78 um against the geometric arrest bound a_0/sqrt(6) = 6.04 um; twinned-area ratio 0.123 against the phi = 0.50 null; k ratio 0.193) and the templating result (IoU 0.753 against 1.0 with the 0.418 flux-matched control in the method string). Deductions: the headline Pass 2 validation — 12-species r = 0.9997 (L1938-1947) — is circular because the table's e_rel_obs equals e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 by construction (-5); the Gibson-Ashby 2.0x at phi = 0.5 (L1988-1997) is the algebraic identity C phi/(C phi^2), chi = -4 (L1978-1987) is a lookup (L446-453) not computed from the field, and Z = 0 (L1998-2007) is assigned via get_tpms_nodal_strut_vectors(\"none\") (L441) (-3); several Pass 3 references are weak: the stiffness ratio reference 0.19 is Gibson-Ashby stretching although the 2D honeycomb is bending-dominated (L1895-1903), the pore-arrest fraction 0.26 vs ideal 1.0 includes notch-singularity elements at hexagon vertices (L1885-1893), the largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 against a reference of 1.0 (the single chance primary-nucleation event at k_1 = 1e-7 seeds a second domain holding 23% of the crystalline pixels; the self-test's `domains <= 2` does not catch this and the Phase A handoff reported it as ~0.999) (L1915-1923), and the ACC-fraction reference 0.0 is asymptotic rather than a literature time point (L1925-1934) (-3); the specimen a_0 reference is self-referential (L2018-2027) (-1). Net -6 from v2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json L86–L98: DEFECT: cross_taxa_echinoderm_stereom_table has no per-row figure/table/DOI provenance; TPMS-type assignments (e.g. Cidaris rugosa 'Primitive P') unsupported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json#L86-L98>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1885–L1903: Pass 3 references of limited strength: pore-arrest ideal 1.0 vs 0.26 (notch-vertex twinning), stiffness ratio reference 0.19 = stretching C phi while the honeycomb section is bending-dominated (GA 2.3 (t/l)^3 = 0.288 noted in the source string) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1885-L1903>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1915–L1923: DEFECT: largest-domain fraction measures 0.766 (measurements.yaml) vs reference 1.0 — a chance primary event seeds a 23% second domain; the self-test's domains <= 2 (L2130) does not catch it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1915-L1923>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1938–L1947: DEFECT: 12-species Pearson r = 0.9997 is circular — reference-table e_rel_obs is e_rel_pred +/- 0.002 for every row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1938-L1947>",
        "models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py L1978–L2007: DEFECT: chi = -4 is a genus lookup (L446-453), 2.0x Gibson-Ashby ratio is the identity C phi/(C phi^2), pinch-off Z = 0 is assigned via the 'none' strut set (L441) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/models/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1978-L2007>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-12-species-echinodermata-tpms-vs-labyrinthic-stereom-relative-modulus-correlation-e-e-s>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-measurement-3d-schwarz-diamond-tpms-implicit-surface-mean-curvature-h-on-zero-level-set>,
