<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature & Non-Positive Gaussian Saddle Curvature Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that zero mean curvature (H = 0) on biogenic TPMS stereom surfaces enforces equal and opposite principal curvatures (kappa_1 = -kappa_2) and strictly non-positive hyperbolic saddle Gaussian curvature (K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0) that eliminates local stress concentrations | Variables: kappa_1, kappa_2: principal curvatures of the calcite-pore interface; H = (kappa_1 + kappa_2)/2: mean curvature; K = kappa_1 * kappa_2: Gaussian curvature" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Schoen (1970) NASA TN D-5541" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L287-L478>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L27-L66> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twice_mean_curvature (k1 k2 : Int) : Int := k1 + k2
def gaussian_curvature (k1 k2 : Int) : Int := k1 * k2
def minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature (k1 : Int) : Int := gaussian_curvature k1 (-k1)
theorem tpms_minimal_surface_zero_mean_curvature_and_nonpositive_gaussian :
    twice_mean_curvature 3 (-3) = 0 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 0 = 0 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 3 = -9 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 3 < 0 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "2 * H = kappa_1 + kappa_2 = 0  =>  kappa_2 = -kappa_1  and  K = kappa_1 * kappa_2 = -kappa_1^2 <= 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_minimal_surface_zero_mean_curvature_and_nonpositive_gaussian" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "TPMS Odd Inversion Symmetry & Exact 50% Bicontinuous Volume Fraction Law at c = 0" ;
    dct:description "Proves that odd inversion symmetry of the TPMS level-set potential partitions the unit cell into congruent solid calcite and pore labyrinths of exact 50% volume fraction at c = 0, with strict monotonic decrease as threshold c increases toward pinch-off | Variables: F(X,Y,Z): nodal TPMS level-set potential; c: level-set isosurface threshold; phi(c): solid calcite volume fraction" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Schoen (1970) NASA TN D-5541" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L504-L544>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L72-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def tpms_odd_field (x y z : Int) : Int := x + y + z
def sym_coords : List Int := [-3, -1, 1, 3]
theorem tpms_odd_inversion_symmetry_and_half_volume_fraction_at_zero :
    tpms_odd_field (-3) (-1) 1 + tpms_odd_field 3 1 (-1) = 0 ∧
    2 * solid_voxel_count 0 = total_voxel_count ∧
    solid_voxel_count (-4) > solid_voxel_count 0 ∧
    solid_voxel_count 0 > solid_voxel_count 4 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F(-X,-Y,-Z) = -F(X,Y,Z)  =>  phi(c = 0) = Vol({F > 0}) / Vol(Omega) = 1/2 = 0.5000,   d(phi)/dc < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.solid_voxel_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_odd_inversion_symmetry_and_half_volume_fraction_at_zero" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Maxwell Nodal Connectivity Valence (Z=4 Diamond Tetrahedral cos theta = -1/3 vs Z=3 Gyroid vs Z=6 Primitive) & Genus-3 Euler Characteristic Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the 4-valent tetrahedral [111] strut geometry (109.4712 deg) of Protoreaster nodosus Diamond stereom vs 3-valent Gyroid (120 deg) and 6-valent Primitive (90 deg) stereom and their shared genus-3 unit-cell topology (chi = -4) | Variables: Z: skeletal strut coordination number at each TPMS vertex node; v_k: tetrahedral [111] strut vectors of Schwarz Diamond stereom; g = 3: topological genus per fundamental cubic unit cell; chi = -4: Euler characteristic" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Donnay & Pawson (1969) Science 166:1147-1150" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L210-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L137-L221> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def diamond_strut : Nat → Vec3Int
  | 1 => { x := 1, y := 1, z := 1 } | 2 => { x := 1, y := -1, z := -1 }
  | 3 => { x := -1, y := 1, z := -1 } | 4 => { x := -1, y := -1, z := 1 } | _ => vec3_zero
theorem tpms_nodal_connectivity_valence_and_diamond_tetrahedral_angle :
    tpms_nodal_valence 1 < tpms_nodal_valence 2 ∧
    diamond_strut_sum = vec3_zero ∧
    3 * vec3_dot (diamond_strut 1) (diamond_strut 2) + vec3_norm_sq (diamond_strut 1) = 0 ∧
    tpms_unit_cell_euler_char 3 = -4 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Z_G = 3 (120 deg) < Z_D = 4 (arccos(-1/3) = 109.4712 deg, sum_{k=1}^4 v_k = 0) < Z_P = 6 (90 deg),   chi_cell = 2 - 2*g = -4 (g = 3)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.diamond_strut_sum" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_nodal_connectivity_valence_and_diamond_tetrahedral_angle" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Modulus Scaling: Stretching-Dominated TPMS (phi^1) vs Bending-Dominated Foam (phi^2)" ;
    dct:description "Demonstrates why stretching-dominated biogenic TPMS stereom (phi^1) achieves more than double the specific stiffness of bending-dominated disordered labyrinthic foam (phi^2) at 50% porosity | Variables: phi in (0, 1): solid calcite volume fraction; E*/E_s: relative Young's modulus normalized by monolithic calcite modulus E_s = 76 GPa; C_stretch, C_bend: Gibson-Ashby geometric constants" ;
    dct:source "Gibson & Ashby (1997) Cellular Solids; Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L978-L1059>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L227-L263> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled (c_coeff phi_pct : Nat) : Nat := c_coeff * 100 * phi_pct
def gibson_ashby_bending_scaled (c_coeff phi_pct : Nat) : Nat := c_coeff * phi_pct * phi_pct
theorem gibson_ashby_stretching_vs_bending_cellular_modulus_scaling :
    gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled 38 50 > gibson_ashby_bending_scaled 38 50 ∧
    gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled 38 50 = 2 * gibson_ashby_bending_scaled 38 50 := by decide
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "E*_TPMS / E_s = C_stretch * phi^1  >  E*_foam / E_s = C_bend * phi^2  for all phi in (0, 1);   at phi = 0.50, E*_TPMS / E*_foam = 2.0 (for C_stretch = C_bend)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.gibson_ashby_stretching_vs_bending_cellular_modulus_scaling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Twin-Lamella Arrest at Strut Free Surfaces & Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro Dislocation Pile-Up Bounded by Glide Length (Pass 3 nanoindentation crystal-plasticity FEM)" ;
    dct:description "Reduced crystal-plasticity model of Yang et al. (2022) nanoindentation: twin bands nucleated under a flat punch in the [111] Diamond lattice section are arrested at strut-pore free surfaces (lamella <= strut chord, twinned area far below the phi-scaled null) whereas the monolithic single crystal develops an extended twin zone; the pile-up scaling bounds dislocation head stress by the strut length | Variables: u: nodal displacements of the plane-strain Q4 mesh; eps_p = sum_v gamma_v sym(s_v (x) n_v): twin plastic strain; tau_twin: effective e-twin CRSS; s_twin = 0.694: calcite e-twin shear; theta = 26.25 deg: e{01-18} pole to c-axis; L: glide/strut length (a_0 sqrt(3)/4 in 3D, a_0/sqrt(6) projected on (111)); mu = E/(2(1+nu)); b = 0.81 nm Burgers vector" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Eshelby, Frank & Nabarro (1951) Phil Mag 42:351-364; Turner, Griggs & Heard (1954) GSA Bull 65:883-934; De Bresser & Spiers (1997) Tectonophysics 272:1-23" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L609-L974>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L255-L315> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twin_lamella_length (free_run strut_chord : Nat) : Nat := min free_run strut_chord
def pileup_count (kappa glide_length tau : Nat) : Nat := kappa * glide_length * tau
def pileup_head_stress (kappa glide_length tau : Nat) : Nat := pileup_count kappa glide_length tau * tau
def clamped_twin_shear (gamma s_twin : Nat) : Nat := min gamma s_twin
theorem twin_lamella_arrest_and_dislocation_pileup_bounded_by_strut_length :
    (∀ f L : Nat, twin_lamella_length f L ≤ L) ∧
    (∀ κ τ L₁ L₂ : Nat, L₁ ≤ L₂ → pileup_head_stress κ L₁ τ ≤ pileup_head_stress κ L₂ τ) ∧
    (∀ γ s : Nat, clamped_twin_shear γ s ≤ s) ∧
    pileup_count 1 6 10 < pileup_count 1 1000 10 := by ...
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "K u = f_p(eps_p) - K_fp u_p,  sigma = D (eps - eps_p),  |tau_rss^(v)| = |sigma : sym(s^(v) (x) n^(v))| <= tau_twin,  |gamma| <= s_twin ;  L_lamella = min(L_free, L_chord) <= a_0/sqrt(6) ;  n = pi (1 - nu) L tau / (mu b),  sigma_head = n tau = pi (1 - nu) L tau^2 / (mu b)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.pileup_head_stress" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.twin_lamella_arrest_and_dislocation_pileup_bounded_by_strut_length" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Syncytial Membrane Templating of ACC Precursor Vesicles, Secondary-Nucleation Single-Crystallinity & Monotone ACC Depletion (Pass 3 larval spiculogenesis)" ;
    dct:description "Models the intracellular syncytial templating of ~1 um ACC vesicles into the stereom shape and the Politi et al. (2008) secondary-nucleation ACC -> calcite transformation that keeps the spicule a single crystal (Donnay & Pawson 1969); templating and nucleation ablations quantify fidelity (IoU 0.75 vs 0.42 untemplated) and polycrystallinity (2 vs 239 domains) | Variables: A: amorphous calcium carbonate field; C: calcite field; T: syncytial membrane template (the [111] Diamond skeletal section); p_in, p_out: vesicle exocytosis acceptance inside/outside the cavity; k_2: secondary-nucleation conversion rate; k_1: primary nucleation probability; n_primary: number of de novo nucleation events" ;
    dct:source "Politi et al. (2008) PNAS 105:17362-17366; Beniash et al. (1997) Proc R Soc B 264:461-465; Vidavsky et al. (2014) PNAS 111:39-44; Donnay & Pawson (1969) Science 166:1147-1150" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1155-L1314>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L317-L379> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def crystal_domain_count (n_primary : Nat) : Nat := 1 + n_primary
def vesicle_accept_weight (inside : Bool) (p_in p_out : Nat) : Nat := if inside then p_in else p_out
def acc_step (a : Nat) : Nat := a - a / 4
def acc_after : Nat → Nat → Nat | 0, a => a | t + 1, a => acc_after t (acc_step a)
theorem syncytial_secondary_nucleation_single_domain_and_acc_depletion :
    crystal_domain_count 0 = 1 ∧
    (∀ a b : Nat, a ≤ b → crystal_domain_count a ≤ crystal_domain_count b) ∧
    (∀ p_in p_out : Nat, p_out ≤ p_in → vesicle_accept_weight false p_in p_out ≤ vesicle_accept_weight true p_in p_out) ∧
    (∀ a : Nat, acc_step a ≤ a) ∧
    acc_after 6 1000 < acc_after 5 1000 := by ...
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P(accept | x) = p_in if x in template else p_out ;  A += vesicle disc (capacity 1 - C) ;  dC = k_2 A on ACC within reach of calcite (domain inherited) ;  primary nucleation w.p. k_1 per ACC-rich pixel opens a new domain ;  domain_count = 1 + n_primary ;  a_{t+1} = a_t - a_t/4 <= a_t ;  IoU = |M AND T| / |M OR T|" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.crystal_domain_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.syncytial_secondary_nucleation_single_domain_and_acc_depletion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature & Non-Positive Gaussian Saddle Curvature Law" ;
    dct:description "Establishes that zero mean curvature (H = 0) on biogenic TPMS stereom surfaces enforces equal and opposite principal curvatures (kappa_1 = -kappa_2) and strictly non-positive hyperbolic saddle Gaussian curvature (K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0) that eliminates local stress concentrations | Variables: kappa_1, kappa_2: principal curvatures of the calcite-pore interface; H = (kappa_1 + kappa_2)/2: mean curvature; K = kappa_1 * kappa_2: Gaussian curvature" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Schoen (1970) NASA TN D-5541" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L287-L478>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L27-L66> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twice_mean_curvature (k1 k2 : Int) : Int := k1 + k2
def gaussian_curvature (k1 k2 : Int) : Int := k1 * k2
def minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature (k1 : Int) : Int := gaussian_curvature k1 (-k1)
theorem tpms_minimal_surface_zero_mean_curvature_and_nonpositive_gaussian :
    twice_mean_curvature 3 (-3) = 0 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 0 = 0 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 3 = -9 ∧
    minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature 3 < 0 := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "2 * H = kappa_1 + kappa_2 = 0  =>  kappa_2 = -kappa_1  and  K = kappa_1 * kappa_2 = -kappa_1^2 <= 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.minimal_surface_gaussian_curvature" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_minimal_surface_zero_mean_curvature_and_nonpositive_gaussian" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "TPMS Odd Inversion Symmetry & Exact 50% Bicontinuous Volume Fraction Law at c = 0" ;
    dct:description "Proves that odd inversion symmetry of the TPMS level-set potential partitions the unit cell into congruent solid calcite and pore labyrinths of exact 50% volume fraction at c = 0, with strict monotonic decrease as threshold c increases toward pinch-off | Variables: F(X,Y,Z): nodal TPMS level-set potential; c: level-set isosurface threshold; phi(c): solid calcite volume fraction" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Schoen (1970) NASA TN D-5541" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L504-L544>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L72-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def tpms_odd_field (x y z : Int) : Int := x + y + z
def sym_coords : List Int := [-3, -1, 1, 3]
theorem tpms_odd_inversion_symmetry_and_half_volume_fraction_at_zero :
    tpms_odd_field (-3) (-1) 1 + tpms_odd_field 3 1 (-1) = 0 ∧
    2 * solid_voxel_count 0 = total_voxel_count ∧
    solid_voxel_count (-4) > solid_voxel_count 0 ∧
    solid_voxel_count 0 > solid_voxel_count 4 := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "F(-X,-Y,-Z) = -F(X,Y,Z)  =>  phi(c = 0) = Vol({F > 0}) / Vol(Omega) = 1/2 = 0.5000,   d(phi)/dc < 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.solid_voxel_count" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_odd_inversion_symmetry_and_half_volume_fraction_at_zero" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Maxwell Nodal Connectivity Valence (Z=4 Diamond Tetrahedral cos theta = -1/3 vs Z=3 Gyroid vs Z=6 Primitive) & Genus-3 Euler Characteristic Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs the 4-valent tetrahedral [111] strut geometry (109.4712 deg) of Protoreaster nodosus Diamond stereom vs 3-valent Gyroid (120 deg) and 6-valent Primitive (90 deg) stereom and their shared genus-3 unit-cell topology (chi = -4) | Variables: Z: skeletal strut coordination number at each TPMS vertex node; v_k: tetrahedral [111] strut vectors of Schwarz Diamond stereom; g = 3: topological genus per fundamental cubic unit cell; chi = -4: Euler characteristic" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Donnay & Pawson (1969) Science 166:1147-1150" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L210-L286>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L137-L221> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def diamond_strut : Nat → Vec3Int
  | 1 => { x := 1, y := 1, z := 1 } | 2 => { x := 1, y := -1, z := -1 }
  | 3 => { x := -1, y := 1, z := -1 } | 4 => { x := -1, y := -1, z := 1 } | _ => vec3_zero
theorem tpms_nodal_connectivity_valence_and_diamond_tetrahedral_angle :
    tpms_nodal_valence 1 < tpms_nodal_valence 2 ∧
    diamond_strut_sum = vec3_zero ∧
    3 * vec3_dot (diamond_strut 1) (diamond_strut 2) + vec3_norm_sq (diamond_strut 1) = 0 ∧
    tpms_unit_cell_euler_char 3 = -4 := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Z_G = 3 (120 deg) < Z_D = 4 (arccos(-1/3) = 109.4712 deg, sum_{k=1}^4 v_k = 0) < Z_P = 6 (90 deg),   chi_cell = 2 - 2*g = -4 (g = 3)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.diamond_strut_sum" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.tpms_nodal_connectivity_valence_and_diamond_tetrahedral_angle" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Modulus Scaling: Stretching-Dominated TPMS (phi^1) vs Bending-Dominated Foam (phi^2)" ;
    dct:description "Demonstrates why stretching-dominated biogenic TPMS stereom (phi^1) achieves more than double the specific stiffness of bending-dominated disordered labyrinthic foam (phi^2) at 50% porosity | Variables: phi in (0, 1): solid calcite volume fraction; E*/E_s: relative Young's modulus normalized by monolithic calcite modulus E_s = 76 GPa; C_stretch, C_bend: Gibson-Ashby geometric constants" ;
    dct:source "Gibson & Ashby (1997) Cellular Solids; Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L978-L1059>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L227-L263> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled (c_coeff phi_pct : Nat) : Nat := c_coeff * 100 * phi_pct
def gibson_ashby_bending_scaled (c_coeff phi_pct : Nat) : Nat := c_coeff * phi_pct * phi_pct
theorem gibson_ashby_stretching_vs_bending_cellular_modulus_scaling :
    gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled 38 50 > gibson_ashby_bending_scaled 38 50 ∧
    gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled 38 50 = 2 * gibson_ashby_bending_scaled 38 50 := by decide
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "E*_TPMS / E_s = C_stretch * phi^1  >  E*_foam / E_s = C_bend * phi^2  for all phi in (0, 1);   at phi = 0.50, E*_TPMS / E*_foam = 2.0 (for C_stretch = C_bend)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.gibson_ashby_stretching_scaled" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.gibson_ashby_stretching_vs_bending_cellular_modulus_scaling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Twin-Lamella Arrest at Strut Free Surfaces & Eshelby-Frank-Nabarro Dislocation Pile-Up Bounded by Glide Length (Pass 3 nanoindentation crystal-plasticity FEM)" ;
    dct:description "Reduced crystal-plasticity model of Yang et al. (2022) nanoindentation: twin bands nucleated under a flat punch in the [111] Diamond lattice section are arrested at strut-pore free surfaces (lamella <= strut chord, twinned area far below the phi-scaled null) whereas the monolithic single crystal develops an extended twin zone; the pile-up scaling bounds dislocation head stress by the strut length | Variables: u: nodal displacements of the plane-strain Q4 mesh; eps_p = sum_v gamma_v sym(s_v (x) n_v): twin plastic strain; tau_twin: effective e-twin CRSS; s_twin = 0.694: calcite e-twin shear; theta = 26.25 deg: e{01-18} pole to c-axis; L: glide/strut length (a_0 sqrt(3)/4 in 3D, a_0/sqrt(6) projected on (111)); mu = E/(2(1+nu)); b = 0.81 nm Burgers vector" ;
    dct:source "Yang et al. (2022) Science 375:647-652; Eshelby, Frank & Nabarro (1951) Phil Mag 42:351-364; Turner, Griggs & Heard (1954) GSA Bull 65:883-934; De Bresser & Spiers (1997) Tectonophysics 272:1-23" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L609-L974>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L255-L315> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twin_lamella_length (free_run strut_chord : Nat) : Nat := min free_run strut_chord
def pileup_count (kappa glide_length tau : Nat) : Nat := kappa * glide_length * tau
def pileup_head_stress (kappa glide_length tau : Nat) : Nat := pileup_count kappa glide_length tau * tau
def clamped_twin_shear (gamma s_twin : Nat) : Nat := min gamma s_twin
theorem twin_lamella_arrest_and_dislocation_pileup_bounded_by_strut_length :
    (∀ f L : Nat, twin_lamella_length f L ≤ L) ∧
    (∀ κ τ L₁ L₂ : Nat, L₁ ≤ L₂ → pileup_head_stress κ L₁ τ ≤ pileup_head_stress κ L₂ τ) ∧
    (∀ γ s : Nat, clamped_twin_shear γ s ≤ s) ∧
    pileup_count 1 6 10 < pileup_count 1 1000 10 := by ...
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "K u = f_p(eps_p) - K_fp u_p,  sigma = D (eps - eps_p),  |tau_rss^(v)| = |sigma : sym(s^(v) (x) n^(v))| <= tau_twin,  |gamma| <= s_twin ;  L_lamella = min(L_free, L_chord) <= a_0/sqrt(6) ;  n = pi (1 - nu) L tau / (mu b),  sigma_head = n tau = pi (1 - nu) L tau^2 / (mu b)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.pileup_head_stress" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.twin_lamella_arrest_and_dislocation_pileup_bounded_by_strut_length" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Syncytial Membrane Templating of ACC Precursor Vesicles, Secondary-Nucleation Single-Crystallinity & Monotone ACC Depletion (Pass 3 larval spiculogenesis)" ;
    dct:description "Models the intracellular syncytial templating of ~1 um ACC vesicles into the stereom shape and the Politi et al. (2008) secondary-nucleation ACC -> calcite transformation that keeps the spicule a single crystal (Donnay & Pawson 1969); templating and nucleation ablations quantify fidelity (IoU 0.75 vs 0.42 untemplated) and polycrystallinity (2 vs 239 domains) | Variables: A: amorphous calcium carbonate field; C: calcite field; T: syncytial membrane template (the [111] Diamond skeletal section); p_in, p_out: vesicle exocytosis acceptance inside/outside the cavity; k_2: secondary-nucleation conversion rate; k_1: primary nucleation probability; n_primary: number of de novo nucleation events" ;
    dct:source "Politi et al. (2008) PNAS 105:17362-17366; Beniash et al. (1997) Proc R Soc B 264:461-465; Vidavsky et al. (2014) PNAS 111:39-44; Donnay & Pawson (1969) Science 166:1147-1150" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py#L1155-L1314>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987db7d/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean#L317-L379> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def crystal_domain_count (n_primary : Nat) : Nat := 1 + n_primary
def vesicle_accept_weight (inside : Bool) (p_in p_out : Nat) : Nat := if inside then p_in else p_out
def acc_step (a : Nat) : Nat := a - a / 4
def acc_after : Nat → Nat → Nat | 0, a => a | t + 1, a => acc_after t (acc_step a)
theorem syncytial_secondary_nucleation_single_domain_and_acc_depletion :
    crystal_domain_count 0 = 1 ∧
    (∀ a b : Nat, a ≤ b → crystal_domain_count a ≤ crystal_domain_count b) ∧
    (∀ p_in p_out : Nat, p_out ≤ p_in → vesicle_accept_weight false p_in p_out ≤ vesicle_accept_weight true p_in p_out) ∧
    (∀ a : Nat, acc_step a ≤ a) ∧
    acc_after 6 1000 < acc_after 5 1000 := by ...
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P(accept | x) = p_in if x in template else p_out ;  A += vesicle disc (capacity 1 - C) ;  dC = k_2 A on ACC within reach of calcite (domain inherited) ;  primary nucleation w.p. k_1 per ACC-rich pixel opens a new domain ;  domain_count = 1 + n_primary ;  a_{t+1} = a_t - a_t/4 <= a_t ;  IoU = |M AND T| / |M OR T|" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0040-1951(96)00273-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139878326>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1665587>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0806604105>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1312833110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1080/14786445108561060>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1997.0066>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.166.3909.1147>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abm8666>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1130/0016-7606(1954)65%5B883:EDOCC%5D2.0.CO;2>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2108/zsj.19.253> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Triply Periodic Minimal Surface (TPMS) Nodal Level-Set Geometry (Schwarz Diamond D, Schoen Gyroid G, Schwarz Primitive P), Minimal Surface Zero Mean Curvature (H = 0, K = -kappa_1^2 <= 0), Gibson-Ashby Cellular Solid Scaling, Plane-Strain Crystal-Plasticity FEM of e-Twin Arrest (Pass 3) & Stochastic Syncytial ACC Templating Kinetics (Pass 3)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.crystal_domain_count" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_079.syncytial_secondary_nucleation_single_domain_and_acc_depletion" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

